# HR Management System

A web-based HR Management System built with **React**, **Spring Boot**, **PostgreSQL**, and **Docker**.

## Technologies

* Frontend: React
* Backend: Spring Boot / Java 17
* Database: PostgreSQL 15
* Containerization: Docker & Docker Compose
* CI/CD: GitHub Actions
* Deployment: Docker Hub + VPS

## Project Structure

```text
HR-Management/
├── frontend/                 # React frontend
├── src/                      # Spring Boot backend
├── dockerfile                # Backend Dockerfile
├── Docker-compose.prod.yml   # Production configuration
├── docker-compose.dev.yml    # Development configuration
├── pom.xml                   # Maven configuration
├── mvnw                      # Maven wrapper
└── package.json
```

## Running in Development

Start the development containers:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d --build
```

The application will be available at:

```text
Frontend: http://localhost:3000
Backend:  http://localhost:8081
Database: localhost:5433
```

Stop the containers:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml down
```

## Running in Production

The production environment uses Docker images from Docker Hub.

First, make sure your `.env` file exists on the server:

```env
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=your-secure-password
```

Pull the latest images:

```bash
docker compose -f Docker-compose.prod.yml pull
```

Start the application:

```bash
docker compose -f Docker-compose.prod.yml up -d
```

Check running containers:

```bash
docker ps
```

Stop the application:

```bash
docker compose -f Docker-compose.prod.yml down
```

## CI/CD

The project uses **GitHub Actions**.

When code is pushed to the `main` branch:

```text
Git Push
   ↓
GitHub Actions
   ↓
Build Backend
   ↓
Build Frontend
   ↓
Build Docker Images
   ↓
Push Images to Docker Hub
   ↓
Deploy to VPS
```

Docker Hub credentials are stored securely as GitHub repository secrets:

```text
DOCKERHUB_USERNAME
DOCKERHUB_TOKEN
```

## Database

PostgreSQL is used as the application database.

Development:

```text
Database: HRS
Username: postgres
Port: 5433
```

Inside Docker, the backend connects to PostgreSQL using:

```text
jdbc:postgresql://postgres:5432/HRS
```

## Production

The production environment should use:

* A strong PostgreSQL password
* HTTPS
* A domain name
* Nginx as a reverse proxy
* Docker Hub images
* GitHub Actions for deployment

